CATEGORIES:Main
CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a009144-7fb64372-017f-f2fa77e0-000007ea:Runton\, R
 ajashi
CREATED:20260616T205019Z
DESCRIPTION:: Immersive computing is emerging as a new computing paradigm 
 that enables applications in domains such as healthcare\, education\, and
  training. However\, developing practical immersive systems remains chall
 enging due to the massive data volume of 3D content and the stringent lat
 ency and reliability requirements of interactive applications. In this ta
 lk\, I will present my research on building scalable and intelligent syst
 ems for immersive computing. First\, I will discuss how to make immersive
  content deliverable under bandwidth constraints using systems such as Vi
 Vo and NeVo\, which exploit the characteristics of point clouds and neura
 l representations to improve streaming efficiency. Next\, I will present 
 M5 and MuV$^2$\, which address the challenges of supporting scalable\, im
 mersive experiences for multiple users over dynamic wireless networks. Fi
 nally\, I will introduce MagicStream and LITE\, which leverage semantic c
 ommunication and multimodal loss recovery to enable low-latency\, high-fi
 delity\, and resilient immersive telepresence. I will conclude with a vis
 ion for reality-centric immersive computing\, highlighting opportunities 
 in human-AI interaction and humanoid teleoperation.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260616T205019Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260702T110000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260616T205019Z
LOCATION;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf6e-00000000:None
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Athena Seminar Series: Toward Scalable\, Real-Time\, and AI-Native
  Immersive Systems
