CREATED:20251208T193656Z
DESCRIPTION:Duke University Libraries will be turning the pages of the Bir
 ds of America on the first Friday of every month! We welcome you to stop 
 by and watch-what bird will be next?\nDue to holiday closures and other c
 omplications this month'e event is canceled. Please join us in August for
  the next page turn! Birds of America is one of the greatest undertakings
  in the history of both art and ornithology. Almost 200 years after its p
 ublication\, it remains a primary resource for scientists and scholars. T
 his four-volume\, double-elephant-folio edition on handmade paper measure
 s three feet tall and two feet wide and comprises 435 hand-colored prints
  impressed from copperplate engravings. Of the original 175 to 200 comple
 te sets\, 125 have survived. Nine species of those depicted have since go
 ne extinct.
DURATION:PT30M
DTSTAMP:20260625T081359Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260703T121500
LAST-MODIFIED:20260625T081359Z
